WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.520
For years, Star Wars fans have dreamed of
seeing some of the saga's many canceled projects,

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.040
from the Underworld TV series to George Lucas'
sequel trilogy.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:14.150
Would they be just as excited for a droid
spin-off or an Ewok video game, though?

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.000
We'll let you decide...

00:00:15.668 --> 00:00:20.250
James Mangold's Boba Fett movie could be the
greatest loss the Star Wars fandom will ever

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.250
suffer.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:25.830
The celebrated director and Academy Award-nominated
writer was the man who delivered the superb

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:30.440
final chapter in Wolverine's cinematic story
with Logan — and there can be no doubt that

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:34.100
he would have brought a fantastic Boba Fett
story to the screen.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.570
Mangold proved with both Logan and 3:10 to
Yuma that he can make modern westerns with

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.960
equal parts brutal action and thematic heft.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:45.870
While The Mandalorian has certainly offered
fans a more western-inspired taste of the

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:51.090
Star Wars universe, a feature would have allowed
Mangold to flesh out a more epic story.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:55.030
This movie might even have been the film that
brought the franchise back into the best screenplay

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.350
category at the Oscars, given Mangold's previous
historic nomination for Logan.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:03.059
Of course, there's no way to know for sure
— but that doesn't make this particular

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:04.250
loss any less painful.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:09.630
A Wookiee-focused movie was an idea that George
Lucas came up with when initially developing

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:15.139
Star Wars; somewhat disastrously, this idea
eventually led to the Star Wars Holiday Special.

00:01:15.139 --> 00:01:19.100
"Whip whip stir, stir, whip, stir, whip whip
whip stir waaaaah!"

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:23.670
But with the right script and a creative director,
this could be something far superior to that

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:24.929
particular outing.

00:01:24.929 --> 00:01:29.909
Lucas' original idea was a film that didn't
focus on Chewbacca, but instead allowed for

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:32.590
a more ethnographic study of Wookiees.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.829
No one knows exactly what the story would
have been, but the Wookiee homeworld of Kashyyyk

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:41.549
[has a significant history of occupations
and uprisings that would lend itself perfectly

00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:43.439
to a Wookiee-focused story.

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:48.429
The movie would likely dive into their culture
while also offering the classic "rebels vs.

00:01:48.429 --> 00:01:52.240
oppressors" storyline that's such a staple
of the Star Wars saga.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:56.119
And based on the battle on Kashyyyk in Revenge
of the Sith, it probably would have looked

00:01:56.119 --> 00:01:57.340
great too.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.990
Of course, you've got to consider the fact
that Wookiees only speak in unintelligible

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:01.990
growls.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:06.380
While this may seem like a problem, it's also
an opportunity for something really exciting

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:07.990
and somewhat avant garde.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:13.930
A lack of spoken dialogue has driven some
fascinating movies, such as 2014's The Tribe,

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:17.330
in which the character's only speak in Ukrainian
sign language.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:21.430
Doing something similar with the Wookiees
could have been a huge success or a terrible

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:23.934
failure… but it would have been fascinating
either way.

00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:29.530
A droid-only movie was another concept for
a one-off film that Lucas had in the '70s

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:33.420
— one that also could have developed into
something truly special for the franchise.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:37.329
The obvious reference point for this kind
of thing is Wall-E, which proved that you

00:02:37.329 --> 00:02:42.409
can tell a story that focused on robots and
still be engaging and emotionally impactful.

00:02:42.409 --> 00:02:46.780
The major differences, of course, are that
Lucas envisioned a movie with no human characters

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:52.060
at all, as well as the fact that many droids
can speak in languages that viewers can understand.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.900
While the film would not have made room for
any human characters, it would have allowed

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:58.459
for comprehensible dialogue between the droids.

00:02:58.459 --> 00:03:02.930
Like the Wookiee-focused movie, the idea here
was not to extend the stories of droids that

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:08.049
viewers knew already, but to tell an entirely
separate story that explored how droids interact

00:03:08.049 --> 00:03:11.470
with one another when other lifeforms aren't
around.

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:15.090
Considering audiences have only been given
glimpses of this kind of thing in existing

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:19.033
films, it's likely that many fans would have
clamored at the chance to see a little more.

00:03:19.624 --> 00:03:23.940
Star Wars: Underworld was a live action TV
series that was going to take fans into the

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.319
murky depths of the Star Wars universe.

00:03:26.319 --> 00:03:30.780
The show promised to be a more adult take
on the saga, offering up fresh and exciting

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:34.040
stories that weren't solely focused on the
Skywalker clan.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.549
It would have taken place between the end
of Revenge of the Sith and the beginning of

00:03:37.549 --> 00:03:40.959
A New Hope and explored the dark underbelly
of Coruscant.

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:42.459
"You wanna buy some death sticks?"

00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:44.390
"You don't want to sell me death sticks."

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.549
"I don't want to sell you death sticks."

00:03:46.549 --> 00:03:47.800
"You want to go home and rethink your life."

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.859
"I want to go home and rethink my life."

00:03:49.859 --> 00:03:54.079
The idea this time, however, was to offer
something much more morally ambiguous and

00:03:54.079 --> 00:03:56.430
narratively complex than the films themselves.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:04:01.110
The small screen format and long form structure
of television storytelling would have allowed

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:03.810
for more dialogue and character driven stories.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:08.370
The creators' ambitions for the show were
impressive, too, with frequent Lucas collaborator

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:10.700
Rick McCallum telling SFX Magazine:

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:15.180
"The shows we aspire to are The Sopranos,
The Wire, Battlestar Galactica, Deadwood,

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.530
all of that group."

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:21.790
While Disney has now moved Star Wars into
the world of prestige TV with The Mandalorian,

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:25.790
that show still feels pretty PG when compared
with the shows McCallum mentioned.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:30.000
For now, we can hope that the fact that The
Mandalorian's runaway success might be a source

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.667
of hope for Underworld's future.

00:04:32.296 --> 00:04:36.470
George Lucas' sequel trilogy would have been
very different from the one Disney ended up

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:37.470
producing.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:41.510
As revealed by Lucas in interviews for the
book The Star Wars Archives, arguably the

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:45.140
most exciting aspect of his trilogy ideas
were the villains.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:49.630
Lucas' big bads would have been Darth Maul
and his new apprentice, the Twi'lekDarth Talon.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:54.360
In these movies, Maul's power would not have
been governmental, but instead criminal.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:58.030
Lucas envisioned a power vacuum after the
fall of the Empire that would have been filled

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:02.710
by Maul, who would have united the criminal
world and become "the godfather of crime in

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:03.710
the universe."

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:07.650
The films also would have placed Leia at the
heart of the story, working to combat Maul's

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.650
influence in the galaxy and rebuild the Republic.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:14.230
Meanwhile, Luke would have been attempting
to rebuild the Jedi Order from the remaining

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:19.570
Jedi who survived Order 66, finding him on
a mission to locate potential Jedi throughout

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:20.570
the galaxy.

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:24.650
The saga would then reveal that it's actually
Leia who is "the chosen one," as she is the

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:28.840
one who brings harmony to the galaxy through
the creation of a true republic.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:32.220
It's almost certain we'll never get to see
these stories play out now that we already

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:37.860
have a sequel trilogy, but with DC and the
MCU both opening multiverses, what's to stop

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:39.510
Star Wars from joining the fun?

00:05:40.297 --> 00:05:45.340
Thanks to the announcement that Lucasfilm
Games are remaking the 2003 classic RPG Knights

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:49.330
of the Old Republic, there have been rumors
abound regarding the long-lost Knights of

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:50.900
the Old Republic III.

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:55.490
Sadly, nothing is yet concrete, and there's
no way to know what the game might look like,

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:58.870
given that it's been more than 15 years since
the last installment.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:03.200
But according to Chris Avellone, lead designer
and writer on Knights of the Old Republic

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:06.410
II, there was always an idea for a third game.

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:10.200
According to him, the story would have focused
on an ancient and even more evil group of

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.200
Sith.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.730
Of course, this won't come as a surprise to
fans of the Old Republic games, considering

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:19.490
the second installment teases a hidden cabal
of "True Sith" on more than one occasion.

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:23.190
Certainly, one of the most exciting aspects
of the third game would be unraveling the

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:28.310
mysteries of these hugely powerful beings,
each of whom was to be given a unique origin

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:29.310
story.

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:33.220
Sadly, no one can be sure whether these ideas
will be a part of Knights of the Old Republic

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:37.945
III even if it does one day appear, but that
won't stop fans from dreaming.

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:43.300
Star Wars 1313 seems like it would have been
the video game equivalent of Underworld, with

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.900
the game even apparently aiming for an M rating.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:50.620
Players would have controlled Boba Fett as
he traversed the 1313th level of Coruscant

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:52.840
and unraveled a massive conspiracy.

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:56.740
Like Underworld, the game would have been
more adult-oriented by virtue of its brutal

00:06:56.740 --> 00:07:01.070
violence — as well as a more complex, character-oriented
story.

00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:04.950
Like the canceled Boba Fett movie, the game
would also have been the first in its medium

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:09.890
to focus solely on the legendary bounty hunter,
as opposed to the many games in which he takes

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:11.690
a more sidelined role.

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:16.230
But unlike the movie, which many thought would
be more of a western story, 1313 was to be

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:21.560
an urban crime story, something resembling
film noir and mafia stories more than any

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.560
western.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:26.440
At this point, however, it seems that nobody
will ever see this game in any form, which

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:28.770
is certainly a real loss to the franchise.

00:07:29.574 --> 00:07:34.160
An animated comedy developed by the creators
of Robot Chicken, Star Wars: Detours actually

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:36.230
has 39 completed episodes.

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:40.150
Apparently, though, it didn't quite fit with
what Disney had in mind for the franchise

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:41.190
when they bought it.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:45.380
That might seem surprising, given the huge
success of the Star Wars Robot Chicken sketches

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:46.750
among fans.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:51.080
Clearly George Lucas was willing to let people
make jokes about his beloved franchise, and

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:55.000
the fans would have loved it too, considering
the trailer makes it clear that the show is

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.870
stuffed with all kinds of references, easter
eggs, and clever jokes.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:07:59.870
"Are not!"

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:00.870
"Are too!"

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:03.080
"Nobody's talking to you, trash can."

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:06.730
It also seems as though Detours would have
been a great way to give more screen time

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:11.800
to characters who only appear briefly in the
movies — such as Dexter Jettster, who, based

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:15.150
on the trailer, seems to have been a main
character on the show.

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:18.760
While co-creator Seth Green has said that
there "isn't an interest" in releasing the

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:23.150
show anymore, fans can still hope that Detours
will eventually see the light of day.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:25.250
Do it for Dexter, Disney.

00:08:26.054 --> 00:08:30.760
Star Wars: Return of the Jedi – Ewok Adventure
was one of two video games developed for release

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.680
alongside Return of the Jedi.

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:37.360
For some reason, though, only its sibling,
Death Star Battle, ever made its way to Ataris.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:41.919
Of course, Ewok Adventure wouldn't be developed
for the Atari today, but the idea of playing

00:08:41.919 --> 00:08:47.010
an entire game as an Ewok is undeniably appealing
— whether the concept is retooled for something

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:50.030
grander or stays as little more than a mobile
game.

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:53.980
For example, it's pretty easy to imagine this
concept being retooled into something like

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:58.770
Little Big Planet, giving players the tools
to create maps that include a variety of traps

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:02.720
and contraptions like those the Ewoks create
in Return of the Jedi.

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:06.260
This could also bring a community aspect to
the game that would allow players to share

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:10.050
their creations and fight together against
the invading Empire.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:13.850
Alternatively, it's very easy to imagine that
the original game would be given a fresher

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:17.160
look while remaining little more than a time-sink
mobile game.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:21.740
Either way, everyone loves Ewoks, and a video
game centering Endor's vicious little teddy

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.612
bears would surely put smiles on a lot of
faces.

00:09:25.432 --> 00:09:29.050
Battle of the Sith Lords was a Star Wars video
game that would have allowed players to take

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:33.860
on the role of a young Darth Maul as he grows
into a more powerful Sith Lord — albeit

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:35.900
not entirely of his own volition.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:39.780
In fact, the game would have delved into how
traumatizing the training of a young Sith

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:44.440
Lord can be, with Maul being kidnapped by
Palpatine as a child and tortured into taking

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:45.730
on the role of his apprentice.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:50.140
Sadly, the development of the game ran into
timeline and lore issues with the franchise's

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:55.310
plans to bring Maul back as a significant
character in the Clone Wars animated TV show.

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:59.140
Once that happened, the game development team
was left with too little information to work

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:03.460
from while also being locked into new canonical
facts about Maul's life.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:08.020
Eventually, after significant development
and a number of shifts in the game's trajectory,

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.640
the game was canceled.

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:13.460
This isn't only a shame because the game would
have further developed the story of a beloved

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:15.440
character, though that is also true.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:19.120
But it's also a loss because Battle of the
Sith Lords could have been one of the franchise's

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:23.580
most significant moves into the realm of horror
— with a key aspect of the game being the

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:27.140
way that Maul used his own fear to manipulate
the fears of others.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:29.210
Sounds pretty cool, don't you think?

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:31.690
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:35.580
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:40.000
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

